      "description": "Watch AFC Wimbledon vs Newport County highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Carabao Cup delivered a spectacle of resilience and late drama on August 8, 2026, as AFC Wimbledon hosted Newport County . Both sides entered the fray looking to secure safe passage to the next round, resulting in a contest that kept spectators guessing until the very last kick. Tense Exchanges in the Opening Half The match began with both teams searching for a rhythm. AFC Wimbledon showed early intent as Ryan Johnson and James Tilley forced Jordan Wright into early saves. Newport County were far from passive, with Harrison Biggins proving to be a constant threat from distance, though his efforts were repeatedly blocked by a resolute home defense. The best chance of the half fell to Aron Sasu , whose close-range effort was brilliantly denied by Wright just before the whistle, ensuring the scores remained level at the break. Second Half Twists and Stoppage Time Heroics The intensity shifted significantly after the restart. In the 67th minute, Newport County were awarded a penalty after Lee Jenkins was fouled, but Nathan Bishop produced a superb save to deny Shaquille Gwengwe . The reprieve was short-lived for the hosts, however, as Yahya Bamba unleashed a stunning strike from outside the box into the top corner in the 71st minute to give Newport the lead. Just as it seemed Newport would hold on, Callum Maycock became the hero for the Dons , firing home from the center of the box in the 90+7th minute after a headed assist from Isaac Ogundere following a corner. Decided from the Penalty Spot With the match ending 1-1 after ninety minutes, a penalty shootout was required to separate the two sides. AFC Wimbledon were clinical from twelve yards, with Marcus Browne , Jayden Stockley , James Tilley , Myles Hippolyte , and Steve Seddon all converting their spot-kicks. While Newport County saw successful efforts from Gerard Garner , Cameron Norman , Ciarán Brennan , and Harrison Biggins , the pressure told in the end. Nathan Bishop capped off a fine individual performance by saving Matt Smith's final penalty, securing a 5-4 shootout victory for the home side."
